      {
        "country": "IN",
        "kind": "analog",
        "summary": "The analog is converting an LLP into a private limited company under Companies Act s.366 (form URC-1, plus fresh incorporation paperwork) — an MCA process fronted by NSWS since mca.gov.in blocks automated access; it is slow and tax-sensitive, so many simply incorporate fresh.",
        "actionUrl": "https://www.nsws.gov.in/",
        "actionLabel": "NSWS (MCA conversion filings)"
      },
      {
        "country": "UK",
        "kind": "analog",
        "summary": "The analog move is incorporating an existing sole trade or partnership into a limited company; HMRC's Incorporation Relief defers the capital gains tax when the business transfers in exchange for shares.",
        "actionUrl": "https://www.gov.uk/incorporation-relief",
        "actionLabel": "HMRC — Incorporation Relief"
      },
      {
        "country": "DE",
        "kind": "analog",
        "summary": "Changing legal form is a statutory Formwechsel under the Umwandlungsgesetz (e.g. UG to GmbH, or GbR into GmbH) — notarized, registered in the Handelsregister, and usually tax-neutral if done under the UmwStG.",
        "actionUrl": "https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/umwg_1995/",
        "actionLabel": "UmwG (conversion law) — full text"
      },
      {
        "country": "FR",
        "kind": "analog",
        "summary": "The classic pre-fundraise move is transforming a SARL into a SAS: an extraordinary shareholders' decision, a commissaire report, amended statuts, then the transformation filed through the guichet unique.",
        "actionUrl": "https://procedures.inpi.fr/",
        "actionLabel": "INPI guichet unique (transformation)"
      }
    ],
